   "1": "Frame 1: the throw starts. The stick {way}, and X or Y again and again"
  },
  "lessons": [
   {
    "title": "The chain grab",
    "text": [
     "A throw at low damage leaves Fox in hitstun on his way down, and he falls fast: the thrower grabs him again before he can act.",
     "Each throw adds damage. The chain ends when hitstun is over before the regrab comes, or when Fox comes down where the thrower cannot be in time."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         0
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 1,
        "from": "start"
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: the throw starts. Nothing pressed"
      },
      "cues": [
       {
        "frames": [
         1,
         "END"
        ],
        "words": "Nothing pressed: thrown again and again",
        "kind": "late"
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "The first frame",
    "text": [
     "Once the damage is high enough, hitstun ends a few frames before the regrab. Mash X or Y through the throw: the jump comes out on the first frame Fox can act.",
     "Down and B does the same with the shine, out on its first frame, which also stops his fall."
